Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:46:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] macOS: find the compiler libraries next to NEO

NEO loads IGC by leaf name (IGC_LIBRARY_NAME, FCL_LIBRARY_NAME from
igc.opencl.h: libigc.2.dylib, libigdfcl.2.dylib). On macOS dlopen() of
a leaf name searches LD_LIBRARY_PATH, DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH and the fallback
paths (/usr/local/lib, /usr/lib) only, not the directory of the image
that calls it, so a staged lib/ directory worked only with
DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH set. SysCalls::dlopen now retries a leaf name that was
not found in the directory of the image it is in (libze_intel_gpu,
libigdrcl or libocloc), where Linux packages put the compiler too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../os_interface/macos/sys_calls_macos.cpp    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/shared/source/os_interface/macos/sys_calls_macos.cpp b/shared/source/os_interface/macos/sys_calls_macos.cpp
index 778adf2cd8..b8b9fbef68 100644
--- a/shared/source/os_interface/macos/sys_calls_macos.cpp
+++ b/shared/source/os_interface/macos/sys_calls_macos.cpp
@@ -180,8 +180,26 @@ int ioctl(int fileDescriptor, unsigned long int request, void *arg) {
     return ::ioctl(fileDescriptor, request, arg);
 }
 
+// A leaf name (the compiler: libigc.2.dylib, libigdfcl.2.dylib) that dlopen() does not find on DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH or
+// the fallback paths is looked for next to this library, as Linux finds it in the same lib directory as NEO.
 void *dlopen(const char *filename, int flag) {
-    return ::dlopen(filename, flag);
+    void *handle = ::dlopen(filename, flag);
+    if (handle || !filename || std::strchr(filename, '/')) {
+        return handle;
+    }
+    static const char anchor = 0;
+    Dl_info info = {};
+    if (!dladdr(&anchor, &info) || !info.dli_fname) {
+        return nullptr;
+    }
+    std::string path(info.dli_fname);
+    const auto slash = path.rfind('/');
+    if (slash == std::string::npos) {
+        return nullptr;
+    }
+    path.resize(slash + 1);
+    path += filename;
+    return ::dlopen(path.c_str(), flag);
 }
 
